      "accent": "#C8621A",
      "source_photo": "IMG_09F88790-2D24-4305-9B6A-12066F67AD54.jpeg",
      "lines": [
        {"id":"GAN-001","mr":"सुखकर्ता दुःखहर्ता वार्ता विघ्नाची ।","ro":"Sukh-kar-taa Dukh-har-taa Vaar-taa Vigh-naa-chee","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-002","mr":"नुरवी पुरवी प्रेम कृपा जयाची ।","ro":"Nur-vee Pur-vee Prem Kru-paa Ja-yaa-chee","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-003","mr":"सर्वांगी सुंदर उटी शेंदुराची ।","ro":"Sar-vaan-gee Sun-dar U-tee Shen-du-raa-chee","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-004","mr":"कंठी झळके माळ मुक्ताफळांची ॥१॥","ro":"Kan-thee Jhal-ke Maal Muk-taa-pha-laan-chee","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-R01","mr":"जय देव जय देव जय मंगलमूर्ती ।","ro":"Jai Dev Jai Dev Jai Man-gal-moor-tee","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"GAN-R02","mr":"दर्शनमात्रे मनकामना पुरती ॥धृ॥","ro":"Dar-shan-maa-tre Man-kaam-naa Pur-tee","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"GAN-005","mr":"रत्नखचित फरा तुज गौरीकुमरा ।","ro":"Rat-na-kha-chit Pha-raa Tuj Gau-ree-ku-ma-raa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-006","mr":"चंदनाची उटी कुंकुमकेशरा ।","ro":"Chan-da-naa-chee U-tee Kun-kum-ke-sha-raa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-007","mr":"हिरेजडित मुकुट शोभतो बरा ।","ro":"Hi-re-ja-dit Mu-kut Sho-bha-to Ba-raa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-008","mr":"रुणझुणती नूपुरे चरणी घागरिया ॥२॥","ro":"Run-jhu-na-tee Noo-pu-re Cha-ra-nee Ghaa-ga-ri-yaa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-009","mr":"लंबोदर पीतांबर फणिवरवंदना ।","ro":"Lam-bo-dar Pee-taam-bar Pha-ni-var-van-da-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-010","mr":"सरळ सोंड वक्रतुंड त्रिनयना ।","ro":"Sa-ral Sond Vak-ra-tund Tri-na-ya-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-011","mr":"दास रामाचा वाट पाहे सदना ।","ro":"Daas Raa-maa-chaa Vaat Paa-he Sa-da-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GAN-012","mr":"संकटी पावावे निर्वाणी रक्षावे सुरवरवंदना ॥३॥","ro":"San-ka-tee Paa-vaa-ve Nir-vaa-nee Rak-shaa-ve Su-ra-var-van-da-naa","type":"verse"}
      ],
      "meaning": "Ganpati is hailed as the maker of happiness and the remover of sorrow, the one who ends all word of obstacles. His devotees are shown his beloved form: vermilion paste over every limb, a necklace of pearls at his throat, a jewelled crown, sandal and saffron, anklets that chime as he moves. The closing verse is the plea the whole aarti builds toward - come to us in danger, protect us at the final hour."
    },
    {
