        {"id":"SHA-002","mr":"वीषे कंठी काळा त्रिनेत्री ज्वाळा ।","ro":"Vee-she Kan-thee Kaa-laa Tri-net-ree Jwaa-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-003","mr":"लावण्यसुंदर मस्तकी बाळा ।","ro":"Laa-van-ya-sun-dar Mas-ta-kee Baa-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-004","mr":"तेथुनिया जल निर्मळ वाहे झुळझुळा ॥१॥","ro":"Te-thu-ni-yaa Jal Nir-mal Vaa-he Jhul-jhu-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-R01","mr":"जय देव जय देव जय श्रीशंकरा ।","ro":"Jai Dev Jai Dev Jai Shree-shan-ka-raa","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"SHA-R02","mr":"आरती ओवाळू तुज कर्पूरगौरा ॥धृ॥","ro":"Aar-tee O-vaa-loo Tuj Kar-poor-gau-raa","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"SHA-005","mr":"कर्पूरगौरा भोळा नयनी विशाळा ।","ro":"Kar-poor-gau-raa Bho-laa Na-ya-nee Vi-shaa-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-006","mr":"अर्धांगी पार्वती सुमनांच्या माळा ।","ro":"Ar-dhaan-gee Paar-va-tee Su-ma-naan-chyaa Maa-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-007","mr":"विभूतीचे उधळण शितिकंठ नीळा ।","ro":"Vi-bhoo-tee-che U-dha-lan Shi-ti-kanth Nee-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-008","mr":"ऐसा शंकर शोभे उमावेल्हाळा ॥२॥","ro":"Ai-saa Shan-kar Sho-bhe U-maa-vel-haa-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-009","mr":"देवी दैत्यी सागरमंथन पै केले ।","ro":"De-vee Dai-tyee Saa-gar-man-than Pai Ke-le","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-010","mr":"त्यामाजी अवचित हळाहळ जे उठिले ।","ro":"Tyaa-maa-jee A-va-chit Ha-laa-hal Je U-thi-le","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-011","mr":"ते त्वां असुरपणे प्राशन केले ।","ro":"Te Twaan A-sur-pa-ne Praa-shan Ke-le","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-012","mr":"नीळकंठ नाम प्रसिद्ध झाले ॥३॥","ro":"Neel-kanth Naam Pra-siddh Jhaa-le","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-013","mr":"व्याघ्रांबर फणिवरधर सुंदर मदनारी ।","ro":"Vyaagh-raam-bar Pha-ni-var-dhar Sun-dar Ma-da-naa-ree","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-014","mr":"पंचानन मनमोहन मुनिजनसुखकारी ।","ro":"Pan-chaa-nan Man-mo-han Mu-ni-jan-sukh-kaa-ree","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-015","mr":"शतकोटीचे बीज वाचे उच्चारी ।","ro":"Shat-ko-tee-che Beej Vaa-che Uch-chaa-ree","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"SHA-016","mr":"रघुकुलटिलक रामदासा अंतरी ॥४॥","ro":"Ra-ghu-kul-ti-lak Raam-daa-saa An-ta-ree","type":"verse"}
      ],
      "meaning": "Shiva is seen in the same breath as terrifying and beautiful - garlanded with the whole cosmos, the poison dark at his throat, fire in his third eye, and the crescent set tenderly on his head, with the pure Ganga running down from it. The aarti moves through Parvati at his side, the scattering of sacred ash, and the churning of the ocean, when the Halahal poison rose and Shiva alone drank it and so became Nilkanth, the blue-throated one. Ramdas signs the last verse: this Lord is held in the devotee's own heart."
    },
    {
