      "lines": [
        {"id":"DAT-001","mr":"त्रिगुणात्मक त्रैमूर्ति दत्त हा जाणा ।","ro":"Tri-gu-naat-mak Trai-moor-ti Dat-ta Haa Jaa-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-002","mr":"त्रिगुणी अवतार त्रैलोक्यराणा ।","ro":"Tri-gu-nee A-va-taar Trai-lok-ya-raa-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-003","mr":"नेति नेति शब्द नये अनुमाना ।","ro":"Ne-ti Ne-ti Shabd Na-ye A-nu-maa-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-004","mr":"सुरवरमुनिजन योगी समाधी न ये ध्याना ॥१॥","ro":"Sur-var-mu-ni-jan Yo-gee Sa-maa-dhee Na Ye Dhyaa-naa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-R01","mr":"जय देव जय देव जय श्रीगुरुदत्ता ।","ro":"Jai Dev Jai Dev Jai Shree-gu-ru-dat-taa","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"DAT-R02","mr":"आरती ओवाळिता हरली भवचिंता ॥धृ॥","ro":"Aar-tee O-vaa-li-taa Har-lee Bhav-chin-taa","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"DAT-005","mr":"सबाह्य अभ्यंतरी तू एक दत्त ।","ro":"Sa-baah-ya Abh-yan-ta-ree Too Ek Datt","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-006","mr":"अभाग्यासी कैची कळेल हे मात ।","ro":"A-bhaag-yaa-see Kai-chee Ka-lel He Maat","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-007","mr":"पराही परतली तेथे कैचा हा हेत ।","ro":"Pa-raa-hee Pa-ra-ta-lee Te-the Kai-chaa Haa Het","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-008","mr":"जन्ममरणाचा पुरलासे अंत ॥२॥","ro":"Jan-ma-ma-ra-naa-chaa Pu-ra-laa-se Ant","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-009","mr":"दत्त येऊनिया उभा ठाकला ।","ro":"Dat-ta Ye-oo-ni-yaa U-bhaa Thaa-ka-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-010","mr":"भावे साष्टांगेसी प्रणिपात केला ।","ro":"Bhaa-ve Saash-taan-ge-see Pra-ni-paat Ke-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-011","mr":"प्रसन्न होऊनि आशीर्वाद दिधला ।","ro":"Pra-sann Ho-oo-ni Aa-sheer-vaad Di-dha-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-012","mr":"जन्ममरणाचा फेरा चुकविला ॥३॥","ro":"Jan-ma-ma-ra-naa-chaa Phe-raa Chu-ka-vi-laa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-013","mr":"दत्त दत्त ऐसे लागले ध्यान ।","ro":"Dat-ta Dat-ta Ai-se Laa-ga-le Dhyaan","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-014","mr":"हरपले मन झाले उन्मन ।","ro":"Har-pa-le Man Jhaa-le Un-man","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-015","mr":"मी तू झाली बोळवण ।","ro":"Mee Too Jhaa-lee Bo-la-van","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"DAT-016","mr":"एका जनार्दनी श्रीदत्तध्यान ॥४॥","ro":"E-kaa Ja-naar-da-nee Shree-dat-ta-dhyaan","type":"verse"}
      ],
      "meaning": "Dattatreya is the three qualities in one form, the ruler of the three worlds, and finally beyond every description - neti, neti, not this, not this. He is outside and inside alike, one single Datta, though the unlucky mind cannot take the news in. The aarti then turns to what actually happens: Datta comes and stands before the devotee, who falls full-length in love, and receives the blessing that ends the wheel of birth and death. In the last verse the meditation has gone so deep that the difference between me and you has quietly been seen off."
    },
