      "lines": [
        {"id":"GHA-001","mr":"घालीन लोटांगण वंदीन चरण ।","ro":"Ghaa-leen Lo-taan-gan Van-deen Cha-ran","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-002","mr":"डोळ्यांनी पाहीन रूप तुझे ।","ro":"Do-lyaan-nee Paa-heen Roop Tu-jhe","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-003","mr":"प्रेमे आलिंगन आनंदे पूजिन ।","ro":"Pre-me Aa-lin-gan Aa-nan-de Poo-jin","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-004","mr":"भावे ओवाळीन म्हणे नामा ॥१॥","ro":"Bhaa-ve O-vaa-leen Mha-ne Naa-maa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-005","mr":"त्वमेव माता च पिता त्वमेव ।","ro":"Twa-me-va Maa-taa Cha Pi-taa Twa-me-va","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-006","mr":"त्वमेव बंधुश्च सखा त्वमेव ।","ro":"Twa-me-va Ban-dhush-cha Sa-khaa Twa-me-va","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-007","mr":"त्वमेव विद्या द्रविणं त्वमेव ।","ro":"Twa-me-va Vid-yaa Dra-vi-nam Twa-me-va","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-008","mr":"त्वमेव सर्वं मम देवदेव ॥२॥","ro":"Twa-me-va Sar-vam Ma-ma De-va-dev","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-009","mr":"कायेन वाचा मनसेंद्रियैर्वा ।","ro":"Kaa-ye-na Vaa-chaa Ma-na-sen-dri-yair-vaa","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-010","mr":"बुद्ध्यात्मना वा प्रकृतिस्वभावात् ।","ro":"Bud-dhyaat-ma-naa Vaa Pra-kru-ti-swa-bhaa-vaat","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-011","mr":"करोमि यद्यत्सकलं परस्मै ।","ro":"Ka-ro-mi Yad-yat-sa-ka-lam Pa-ras-mai","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-012","mr":"नारायणायेति समर्पयामि ॥३॥","ro":"Naa-raa-ya-naa-ye-ti Sa-mar-pa-yaa-mi","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-013","mr":"अच्युतं केशवं रामनारायणं ।","ro":"A-chyu-tam Ke-sha-vam Raa-ma-naa-raa-ya-nam","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-014","mr":"कृष्णदामोदरं वासुदेवं हरिम् ।","ro":"Krish-na-daa-mo-da-ram Vaa-su-de-vam Ha-rim","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-015","mr":"श्रीधरं माधवं गोपिकावल्लभं ।","ro":"Shree-dha-ram Maa-dha-vam Go-pi-kaa-val-la-bham","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-016","mr":"जानकीनायकं रामचंद्रं भजे ॥४॥","ro":"Jaa-na-kee-naa-ya-kam Raam-chan-dram Bha-je","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"GHA-017","mr":"हरे राम हरे राम राम राम हरे हरे ।","ro":"Ha-re Raam Ha-re Raam Raam Raam Ha-re Ha-re","type":"refrain"},
        {"id":"GHA-018","mr":"हरे कृष्ण हरे कृष्ण कृष्ण कृष्ण हरे हरे ॥","ro":"Ha-re Krish-na Ha-re Krish-na Krish-na Krish-na Ha-re Ha-re","type":"refrain"}
      ],
      "meaning": "This is the prayer that closes the aarti, and it climbs in four steps. Sant Namdev begins with the body: I will throw myself full-length before you, worship your feet, look my fill at your form, embrace you and wave the lamp. Then the Sanskrit takes over and widens: you alone are mother, father, brother, friend, learning and wealth - you are everything to me. Then whatever I do, with body, speech, mind or senses, I lay at Narayana's feet. It ends in pure names - Achyuta, Keshava, Krishna, Rama - and the Hare Rama Hare Krishna, where nothing is asked for at all."
    },
