      "lines": [
        {"id":"MAN-001","mr":"ॐ यज्ञेन यज्ञमयजन्त देवास्तानि धर्माणि प्रथमान्यासन् ।","ro":"Om Yag-nye-na Yag-nya-ma-ya-jan-ta De-vaas-taa-ni Dhar-maa-ni Pra-tha-maan-yaa-san","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-002","mr":"ते ह नाकं महिमानः सचन्त यत्र पूर्वे साध्याः सन्ति देवाः ॥१॥","ro":"Te Ha Naa-kam Ma-hi-maa-nah Sa-chan-ta Yat-ra Poor-ve Saadh-yaah San-ti De-vaah","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-003","mr":"ॐ राजाधिराजाय प्रसह्य साहिने ।","ro":"Om Raa-jaa-dhi-raa-jaa-ya Pra-sah-ya Saa-hi-ne","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-004","mr":"नमो वयं वैश्रवणाय कुर्महे ।","ro":"Na-mo Va-yam Vai-shra-va-naa-ya Kur-ma-he","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-005","mr":"स मे कामान् कामकामाय मह्यम् ।","ro":"Sa Me Kaa-maan Kaa-ma-kaa-maa-ya Mah-yam","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-006","mr":"कामेश्वरो वैश्रवणो ददातु ।","ro":"Kaa-mesh-wa-ro Vai-shra-va-no Da-daa-tu","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-007","mr":"कुबेराय वैश्रवणाय महाराजाय नमः ॥२॥","ro":"Ku-be-raa-ya Vai-shra-va-naa-ya Ma-haa-raa-jaa-ya Na-mah","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-008","mr":"ॐ स्वस्ति ।","ro":"Om Swas-ti","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-009","mr":"साम्राज्यं भौज्यं स्वाराज्यं वैराज्यं पारमेष्ठ्यं राज्यं महाराज्यमाधिपत्यमयम् ।","ro":"Saam-raaj-yam Bhauj-yam Swaa-raaj-yam Vai-raaj-yam Paa-ra-mesh-thyam Raaj-yam Ma-haa-raaj-ya-maa-dhi-pat-ya-ma-yam","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-010","mr":"समन्तपर्यायी स्यात्सार्वभौमः सार्वायुष आन्तादापरार्धात् ।","ro":"Sa-man-ta-par-yaa-yee Syaat-saar-va-bhau-mah Saar-vaa-yu-sha Aan-taa-daa-pa-raar-dhaat","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-011","mr":"पृथिव्यै समुद्रपर्यन्ताया एकराळिति ॥३॥","ro":"Pru-thiv-yai Sa-mud-ra-par-yan-taa-yaa E-ka-raa-li-ti","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-012","mr":"तदप्येष श्लोकोऽभिगीतो मरुतः परिवेष्टारो मरुत्तस्यावसन् गृहे ।","ro":"Ta-dap-ye-sha Shlo-ko-bhi-gee-to Ma-ru-tah Pa-ri-vesh-taa-ro Ma-rut-tas-yaa-va-san Gru-he","type":"verse"},
        {"id":"MAN-013","mr":"आविक्षितस्य कामप्रेर्विश्वेदेवाः सभासद इति ॥४॥","ro":"Aa-vik-shi-tas-ya Kaa-ma-prer-vish-we-de-vaah Sa-bhaa-sa-da I-ti","type":"verse"}
      ],
      "meaning": "Mantra Pushpanjali is the handful of flowers offered at the very end of worship, and it is Vedic rather than devotional in tone. The first verse says that the gods worshipped through sacrifice, and those were the first sacred laws - and by them the worshippers reached the heights where the ancient ones dwell. The second salutes Vaishravana, Kubera, lord of abundance, asking that wishes worth wishing be granted. The third is the great blessing: sovereignty of every kind, extending over the whole earth to the sea, for a full span of life. The fourth remembers King Marutta, in whose house the Maruts themselves served and the Vishvedevas sat in assembly."
    }
  ]
